     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The example in the FAQ:</div><div><br></div><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-users/4gv3fNCqSNk/J6ZItL2ZJ-IJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-users/4gv3fNCqSNk/J6ZItL2ZJ-IJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467464621000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3q6TsT6Y54qoNAh_-nvIae\">https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-users/4gv3fNCqSNk/J6ZItL2ZJ-IJ</a><br><div><br></div><div>is very helpful, but I got stuck with syntax issues when I tried to use it:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   <br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># beta ~ normal(mu, tau); # does not compile</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>As noted in the FAQ, the implicitly vectorized form gives a compile error. One has to use the explicit notation or a loop. It&#39;s a bit confusing because the FAQ looks like real code. </div></div><div><br></div><div>Dieter</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
